      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed. My intent with `MakeFromCompleteStream` was to make the complete-data contract explicit and to avoid inferring completeness from generic `SkStream` state. Blink also needed the original stream to stay alive because `SkiaImageDecoderBase` keeps a raw pointer to the `SegmentStream`.\n\nBut I agree the two-input Skia API is not ideal: passing both `stream` and `data` creates an unnecessary coherency question about which one is the source of truth.\n\nI simplified this so Skia uses the existing `Decode(sk_sp\u003cconst SkData\u003e)` / `MakeFromData(...)` complete-data path again. Blink now owns the lifetime issue locally by retaining the original stream while calling the existing `SkData` overload. This keeps the Skia API smaller and avoids passing two sources of truth into Skia.",
